# =============================================================================
# CommandAtlas — .gitignore
# Aligned with .ai/ARCHITECTURE.md §11 (folder structure) and
# .ai/ENGINEERING_RULES.md. Do NOT add .ai/ here — it is committed documentation,
# not a build artifact. See .ai/CHANGELOG.md if this file's scope ever changes.
# =============================================================================

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
apps/web/node_modules/
apps/server/node_modules/
packages/shared/node_modules/
.pnp/
.pnp.js
.yarn/cache
.yarn/unplugged
.yarn/build-state.yml
.yarn/install-state.gz

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Next.js (apps/web)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
apps/web/.next/
apps/web/out/
.next/
out/
apps/web/.vercel/
.vercel/
next-env.d.ts

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output — generated/ is reproducible from content/ via
# `npm run build-content` (ARCHITECTURE.md §2). Never hand-edited, never the
# source of truth, and not committed by default. If a release process needs to
# commit generated output as versioned release artifacts instead, do that via
# a tagged release branch — not by removing this ignore rule wholesale.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
generated/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Environment variables & secrets — never committed, per
# ENGINEERING_RULES.md §12. .env.example is intentionally NOT ignored.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
apps/web/.env
apps/web/.env.local
apps/server/.env
apps/server/.env.local
!.env.example
!apps/web/.env.example
!apps/server/.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Logs
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
logs/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Testing (apps/web/e2e, apps/server/tests — per ARCHITECTURE.md §11)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
coverage/
.nyc_output/
apps/web/playwright-report/
apps/web/test-results/
apps/web/blob-report/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IndexedDB / local dev artifacts that sometimes leak into a repo via
# browser-automation tooling (Playwright user-data dirs, etc.)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
apps/web/.playwright/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TypeScript build info — should never exist in this project (no TypeScript,
# per ENGINEERING_RULES.md §1 and §15), but ignored defensively in case a
# dependency's tooling generates one incidentally.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editor / IDE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS files
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# MongoDB local dev artifacts (if run locally instead of Atlas)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
data/db/
*.mongo.lock

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Misc build/dist output for packages/shared or any future package
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal AI/architecture documentation — kept local-only by choice, not
# pushed to the public repo. Every AI coding tool (Claude, Copilot, Cursor,
# Antigravity/Gemini) reads this from local disk regardless of git tracking,
# so nothing functional is lost by ignoring it — this only affects what's
# visible in the pushed repo and its history.
#
# IMPORTANT: if you clone this repo onto a second machine, or anyone else
# clones it, .ai/ will NOT come with it, since it was never committed. Keep a
# backup copy (e.g. in a private repo, a private git submodule, or synced via
# your own means) if you rely on it across multiple machines.
#
# Before making this repo public, decide deliberately whether .ai/ should be
# published as real documentation (many real open-source projects do this and
# it reads as engineering rigor, not as a liability) or stay excluded
# permanently — don't let this default persist by accident once the project
# is no longer solo/private.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.ai/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Explicitly NOT ignored (documented here so it's never accidentally added
# above by a future broad pattern like a stray "*ai*" or ".*"):
#   content/        — committed Markdown, canonical content source of truth
#   scripts/        — committed build pipeline source
#   packages/shared — committed schema/constants source
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------